course: dictionary
lesson: 12503
title: Deplete: using up a resource
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To deplete something means to use so much of it that much less is left. Think of a fuel tank: every mile you drive depletes it a little. «Overfishing has depleted fish stocks» means so many fish were caught that far fewer are left in the sea.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Deplete often comes before things we can run out of, like water, energy, coal or fish. Try swapping in "used up a lot of": «Playing football all afternoon depleted my energy, so I ate two bananas.» My energy went down because I used it up.
explain: Deplete is a verb, so it changes its ending: deplete, depletes, depleted, depleting. «The campers depleted their water on the hot hike» tells us they used up all the water they had, so they had much less left.
fact: «Deplete» means to use up a large amount of something so that there is much less left.
fact: Oil, coal, forests, fish and fresh water are natural resources, and people can deplete them.
fact: Chemicals called CFCs depleted the ozone layer, so they were banned in 1987 under the Montreal Protocol.
fact: The ozone layer is slowly recovering, which shows that damage can be repaired.
fact: Exercise depletes your energy, and eating and drinking refill it.
exercise: «Overfishing has depleted fish stocks.» What does depleted mean here? | Counted every single day | Moved to a new sea | Made bigger and stronger | *Used up, so much less is left
exercise: Running a long race depletes energy. What should Ella do afterwards to refill it? | Run the race again straight away | *Eat and drink to refill her energy | Stop breathing for a while | Sit still and do nothing
exercise: Which word shows the past tense of deplete? | depletes | *depleted | depleting | depletion
test: «The forest was depleted by years of logging, and now many trees are gone.» What does depleted mean? | Planted with new trees | *Used up, so much less is left | Full of animals | Painted green
test: Miss Patel said the lake was ___ after the long dry summer. Which word fits best? | *depleted | ancient | cheerful | enormous
exam: The phrase «severely depleted» means which of these? | *Used up so badly that very little is left | Brand new and shiny | Very well stocked and full | Very expensive to buy
